{
  "_doc": "What every GuildMaster building type looks like in 3D, by level (1-3) and variant, for scripts/building_types.gd -> HouseBuilder (docs/construccion.md). A level is a fragment of a HouseBuilder def merged over `base` and the type's `base`. Tokens the script resolves: colours by name (`colors`); cells \"beside\" (the front cells next to the door), \"beside1\" (the first of them), \"door\"; side \"yard:<sides in order of preference>\" (the first of those sides with enough yard cells behind it: `min`, default 1; the entry is dropped if there is none), with \"run\": true (from/to = that run of yard cells, at most `max`) or cell \"run0\" / \"run1\" / \"runN\" (first, second, last cell of the run); floor \"top\"; court gate \"street\". Variants (picked by seed): `palette`, `mirror` (the yard on the other side), `turn` (ridge along the front when the kit has that roof), `upper_window` (window kind of the storeys over the ground floor) and any def key. `take`: how many metres the house leaves free of the lot's width and depth at that level (the yard: sheds, ovens and yard things only go where there is yard). `lot`: the footprint of data/buildings/<type>.json at 2 m a tile, front x depth. `look` (per type): {roof, plaster, wood, stone} over the variant's palette, what tells the trade apart from afar in a town (every trade has a roof of its own: the houses keep the kit's tile and roof_oscura; roof_verdosa, roof_ocre, roof_granate, roof_musgo, roof_hollin, roof_losa and roof_paja come from tools/p3b_tejas.py); `sign_scale` (file or type): size of the hanging sign. `banner` {emblem, color}: the guild banner on the gable (a colour of `colors`, or none for plain canvas). Balcony from / to may be \"door\", \"door-1\", \"door+1\".",
